JSP(Java Server Pages) Overview:
JSP, or Java Server Pages, is a server-side technology used in Java web
development to create dynamic web content. It allows developers to embed
Java code directly within HTML, XML, or other document types, facilitating
the generation of dynamic and interactive web pages.
Key aspects of JSP in Java:
• Extension of Servlets:
JSP technology is built upon Java Servlets. While Servlets handle the core
processing logic, JSPs provide a more convenient way to manage the presentation
layer by integrating Java code within the markup language.

